{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.frobenius_antipode_unifies","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobenius_antipode_unifies","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frobenius_antipode_unifies","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobenius_antipode_unifies","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/frobenius_antipode_unifies.lean#L64-L74","doc":"**Synthesis statement** of `thm:frobenius-antipode-unifies-…`:\nthe antipode `S = (·)⁻¹` simultaneously satisfies the\ngenerator identity and the anti-homomorphism law that the chirality\n(Term 5) and neutron-tower derivations both invoke. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:frobenius-antipode-unifies-chirality-and-tower","label":"thm:frobenius-antipode-unifies-chirality-and-tower","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-antipode-unifies-chirality-and-tower.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/frobenius_antipode_unifies.lean#L51-L62","doc":"**Antipode fixes the averaged `ud`-pair.**\n\nThe manuscript notes `S` fixes the \"averaged\" pair\n`(1, −h/2) = ½(σ + σ⁻¹)`.  Structurally this is the statement that\nthe antipode is an **involution** (`S∘S = id`), so the symmetric\ncombination `½(g + S g)` is `S`-invariant: applying `S` swaps `g` and\n`S g`, and `S(S g) = g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode_antihom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode_antihom","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/frobenius_antipode_unifies.lean#L42-L49","doc":"**Antipode is an anti-homomorphism** `S(a·b) = S(b)·S(a)`.\n\nThis is the standard group identity `(a·b)⁻¹ = b⁻¹·a⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode_generator","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/frobenius_antipode_unifies.lean#L33-L40","doc":"**Antipode on generators** `S(σᵢ) = σᵢ⁻¹`.\n\nFor the braid generators `σ : ℕ → G` (units of the Hecke algebra),\nthe antipode sends `σᵢ` to `σᵢ⁻¹` — true by definition of\n`frobeniusAntipode`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusAntipode","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/frobenius_antipode_unifies.lean#L29-L31","doc":"The Frobenius antipode realised as the group-inverse map on the\nunit group of the Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0}]}